  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting a second Voice of Victory (1/3) on turn 3 when already having one on the battlefield is a legendary-agnostic play, but more importantly, the opponent has a Stormchaser's Talent with an Otter token (prowess 1/1) and only Steam Vents untapped. Casting Floodpits Drowner at flash speed during combat or on the opponent's turn would be more flexible - it could tap down a blocker or an attacker, and holds up the option to react. Additionally, playing High Noon (each player can't cast more than one spell per turn) could be very strong here since the opponent is playing a spell-heavy Izzet strategy with Stormchaser's Talent. High Noon would severely limit their ability to chain spells and trigger prowess multiple times. However, Voice of Victory's 'opponents can't cast spells during your turn' effect is also powerful, and having two copies provides redundancy. The choice is debatable but High Noon seems like a stronger lock piece in this matchup.",
      "action_taken": "Cast a second Voice of Victory",
      "better_line": "Cast High Noon to lock the opponent to one spell per turn, which is devastating against a prowess/spells strategy. Alternatively, hold mana open for Floodpits Drowner at flash speed to interact with the opponent's creatures.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 34,
      "player": "Qwen3 Rivals",
      "decision_index": 17,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Played Mountain instead of Spirebluff Canal. With only 2 other lands in play (Steam Vents and Island), Spirebluff Canal would enter untapped and provide both U and R mana. Mountain only provides R. Since Spirebluff Canal enters tapped with 3+ other lands, this was the optimal time to play it. Playing Mountain now means Spirebluff Canal will likely enter tapped on a future turn.",
      "action_taken": "Played Mountain (only produces R)",
      "better_line": "Play Spirebluff Canal, which enters untapped with 2 or fewer other lands and produces both U and R, preserving Mountain for a later turn when Spirebluff Canal would enter tapped",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 75,
      "player": "GPT5m Timmy",
      "decision_index": 29,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to use Agna Qel'a's loot ability ({2}{U}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card) with unused mana in postcombat main. This is a pure-upside mana sink that provides card selection at no real cost. Additionally, could have cast Floodpits Drowner to tap down Fear of Missing Out and prevent any delirium/extra combat shenanigans on opponent's turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without using any abilities or casting any spells, leaving mana completely unused.",
      "better_line": "Activate Agna Qel'a to loot for card selection, and/or cast Floodpits Drowner to tap Fear of Missing Out with a stun counter, neutralizing the opponent's only creature.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 89,
      "player": "Qwen3 Rivals",
      "decision_index": 37,
    }
  ],
